# 📄 AI Resume ATS Analyzer

Upload a resume (PDF, DOCX, TXT, or a PNG/JPG photo), optionally paste a job description, and get:

- An **estimated ATS score** (0-100) with a 5-part breakdown
- **Matched and missing keywords**
- **Prioritised improvements** (High / Medium / Low)
- **Bullet-point rewrites** based on your real bullets
- Formatting problems that can trip up ATS parsers
- A downloadable JSON report

Built with **Streamlit** and **Google Gemini Flash**.

> The score is an AI-based estimate, not the output of a real ATS.

## How the score works

Gemini rates five categories from 0-100. The app then computes the overall score itself, so it is consistent:

| Category | Weight |
|---|---|
| Keyword & skills match | 30% |
| Experience & impact | 25% |
| Formatting & parseability | 20% |
| Section completeness | 15% |
| Language & clarity | 10% |

## Run locally

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/ats-resume-analyzer.git
cd ats-resume-analyzer
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
```

Get a free Gemini API key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey, then either:

- paste it into the "Gemini API key" box on the main page, or
- set it as an environment variable: `export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key"`, or
- create `.streamlit/secrets.toml` containing `GEMINI_API_KEY = "your-key"`

## Deploy on Streamlit Community Cloud

1. Push this repo to GitHub.
2. Go to https://share.streamlit.io and sign in with GitHub.
3. Click **Create app**, choose the repo, branch `main`, and main file `app.py`.
4. Open **Advanced settings → Secrets** and add:
   ```toml
   GEMINI_API_KEY = "your-key"
   ```
5. Click **Deploy**.

## Project structure

```
app.py            # Streamlit app
requirements.txt  # Dependencies
README.md
.gitignore        # Keeps secrets out of Git
```

## Notes

- Scanned or image-only resumes are read by Gemini (OCR) automatically, but real ATS software can't do that - export a text-based PDF/DOCX before applying.
- Resume text is sent to Google's Gemini API. Don't upload anything you aren't comfortable sharing.
- The default model is `gemini-flash-latest` (always Google's newest stable Flash). You can change it in the sidebar, e.g. `gemini-2.5-flash`. If a model name is wrong, the app automatically falls back to a working one.
